Z||000006||maryjane||10-24-2001||09:18 PM||||Lone Ranger, Gunga Din, Johhny Weismuller was Tarzan, Heckel & Jeckel.Back when everybody rode the bus to school.<BR>You could discipline your kids without getting sued or arrested.<P>You actually knew everybody on your street.<BR>You had to wait for your burger to be cooked, & it came in a basket with fries on the side, not in a cardboard box.<BR>A grade below 70 was failing.<BR>Nobody but classical fans listened to FM. You had only 3 channels on TV, Had to get up to change channels, and then somebody probably had to go out & rotate the antenna.<BR>As Merle Haggard said, "Before microwave ovens. When a woman could still cook; still would." (no offense, ladies)||||reg||1
Z||000007||Cooter||10-24-2001||09:25 PM||||Hugh, you are showing a little grey with those prices  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>The cheapest I can remember gas was 79 cents and movies were $1.50<BR>A 12oz. Coke was 20 cents in the day care vending machine and Star Blazers was the thing to watch after school. "Play clothes" were on the way out and cable television was a new thing in the 'hood. Textured carpet and wood paneling were your only choices in home decor and there was a Pacer/Gremlin looking car as "the car of the future" at the World's Fair- turns out that we call it a Taurus these days! Tyco train sets and b.b. guns (you'll shoot your eye out!) were under the tree. Skating on hardwood floors with your "Sunday socks" was pretty fun. How about spending a Saturday afternoon digging Coke bottles out of the the ditches around the block and getting a nickel for each one at the IGA supermarket? Suddenly, I have a warm fuzzy feeling all over. D@mn Depends must be leaking again!||||reg||1
Z||000008||Fierowrecker||10-24-2001||09:49 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LZeitgeist:<BR><B>"Ethel...!! You git cher clothes on...!!..."</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>NO, NO, NO...<BR>That were the 70's...<BR>Back further, you would ask the attendant {remember, the guy who pumped the gas??},<BR>"Do you pump Ethel??"||||reg||1
