Z||000022||Wolfhound||10-25-2001||07:37 AM||||Tv was not broadcast until 3:00 PM.<BR>Pinky Lee.<BR>Howdy Doody<BR>Nickel Cokes Back when money was money!<P>Oh yeah! In 1963 the list price for a (new) Corvette was $4200.00!<p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 10-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000023||SteveJ||10-25-2001||09:07 AM||||Remember "gas wars"? We got gas around here at 5 gallons / dollar.<P>Remember filing points? Were we really so poor we couldn't replace them? It was a different mindset wasn't it? Things were expected to last.<P>Remember waiting for the car radio to heat up?<P>Rear view mirrors mounted on the dash? Applying you own outside one by clamping it on the door frame?<P>The kingpin was a maintance item.||||reg||1
Z||000024||JSocha||10-25-2001||10:24 AM||||<UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>The world was flat.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><BR><LI>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif">  Dinasours roamed the earth.<BR><LI>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  Brylcream was for hair!?!?!?!  Now that explains why I hated the taste so much when I brushed my teeth!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><LI>Pop/beer cans were metal not aluminum.<BR><LI>You had a pull tab on the cans that actually came off the can.<BR><LI>Then the cans went to several styles of alum-d-dum.<BR><LI>Then you had the little dots you pushed in that replaced the tab.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  Those little dots sucked!<BR><LI>TAB...Just 1 Calorie was the popular drink right next to SHASTA and/or ELF soda (0.10 a can) and WEIGHT WATCHERS pop.<BR><LI>Captain Kangaroo was the popular childs show in the morning along with Mr. Green Jeans and "Well you know my name is Simon...and the things I draw come true...Oh Take me, take me over to the land of view".<BR><LI>Nuns still slapped your fingers with a ruler.<BR><LI>Mom enrolled you in "her mandatory" Piano lessons to use the Piano that has been collecting dust since she bought it!<BR><LI>Holiday shopping in a small town was nastalgic as everyone visited everyone while shopping and wished you happy holidays versus today's MALLS. &lt;sigh&gt; Christmas is right around the corner.<BR><LI>Christmas decorations were not put up in the stores until after Thanksgiving or the first day of December. Not like today where they are practically being put up in July.<BR><LI>Dad could get pulled over and talk to the officer while he had a beer in his lap and was sipping it between conversations.<BR><LI>Crew cuts were something you absolutely hated.<BR><LI>Family picinics were more common place along with other families on weekends.<BR><LI>Parents didn't have to work on the weekends, especially Sunday.<BR><LI>"Big Boy" burger joints and "A&W's" were all over the place and the comercials rocked!<BR></UL><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by JSocha (edited 10-25-2001).]||||reg||12
Z||000025||LZeitgeist||10-25-2001||12:13 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>If you remember the 70's, you weren't really there.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I was born in '68... I was too young to buy drugs legally.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <BR>||||reg||1
