Z||000033||hugh||10-25-2001||07:27 PM||||I remember waking up to a cold house every morning in the winter.My father had to go stoke the coal stove and add more coal.We lived in Philly and had an outhouse,only it was connected to the house.We had to go out the shed door to get to the toilet,and that was bad when there was snow on the ground.My father got the idea to cut a hole in the wall that we could walk through,the only problem with that was,if the shed door was open and someone opened the front door you could see people on the street as you were sitting on the john.I think most people younger than me don't even know what it is like to wake up cold every morning.(and i'm glad) ||||reg||1
