Z||000037||SKIDMARK||10-26-2001||01:25 AM||||BAZOOKA bubble gum - 2 for a penny<BR>Walking barefoot up hill to..and from school in 3 feet of snow.<BR>A weekly bath, whether you needed it or not.<BR>Maypo....ARG!<BR>Riding in Grandpa's rumble seat.<BR>Trips to the well to get water.<BR>POC beer (Pride Of Cleveland)...ARG!<BR>78 rpm records.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000038||hugh||10-26-2001||07:03 AM||||I remember green stamps.I worked for a supermarket chain.The regular price for something like Idaho potatoes was 29 cents.They would go on sale for 19 cents and we would sell more.If we had green stamps on them(valued at about 1/2 cent),we couldn't keep them on the shelf.I got a Remington nylon22 rifle for 17 1/2 books. I WANT MY MAYPO!||||reg||1
