Z||000049||Sage||10-27-2001||08:35 AM||||Yeah, and no cell phones.  Unless you wanna count the s/w, c/b or ham radios, I know Friiday had one in his cruiser...Dom de dom dom.  Party lines were a constant source of entertainment. <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Have a good one!||||reg||1
Z||000050||Phil||10-27-2001||08:37 AM||||Radios with tubes yet.||||reg||1
Z||000051||Sage||10-27-2001||09:30 AM||||Gassy tubes more often than not!  Remember, you could take your tubes down to the local drug store, or at least the Radio Shack and they had a tester right there out on the floor?  You'd stand there and find the right number and pin configuration, then stick your tube in to test it?  Then you opened up the bottom door on the tester, to get the ones you needed, cause that's where they stored the replacement stock.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000052||hugh||10-27-2001||04:21 PM||||In 52 we moved from Philly to Kirkwood NJ.To make a phone call all we did was pick up the phone and give the operator the last 4 numbers of the person we wanted to call.<BR> Raydar,If color television had come out sooner I wouldn't have 5 kids.We didn't have color,and it was too dark to read.||||reg||14
